# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ACTION REQUIRED — Square deposit payments
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local dev (already gitignored via *.local /
# .dev.vars — see note below), and add the SAME values in the Netlify
# dashboard under Site settings → Environment variables before deploying.
#
# Where to find these values: https://developer.squareup.com/apps
#   1. Open your application in the Square Developer Dashboard
#   2. "Credentials" tab → Application ID + Access Token
#      (there's a separate Sandbox and Production set — use Sandbox to test,
#      Production only once you're ready to take real payments)
#   3. "Locations" tab (or Square Dashboard → Account & Settings → Locations)
#      → Location ID for the salon
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# "sandbox" for testing with fake cards, "production" to charge real cards.
# Set BOTH of these to the same value (client + server read separately):
VITE_SQUARE_ENV=sandbox
SQUARE_ENV=sandbox

# Public — safe to expose in the browser bundle.
VITE_SQUARE_APP_ID=YOUR_SQUARE_APPLICATION_ID
VITE_SQUARE_LOCATION_ID=YOUR_SQUARE_LOCATION_ID

# Secret — server-side only (Netlify function). Do NOT prefix with VITE_ or it
# will be bundled into the public site. Never commit the real value.
SQUARE_ACCESS_TOKEN=YOUR_SQUARE_ACCESS_TOKEN

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE: .env / .env.local are gitignored — safe to put real values in a local
# `.env` file. Never commit real credentials to this file (.env.example).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
